@@ -140,7 +140,7 @@ A song owns its chain: every cue its song cue runs on into by a follow or a hang
 
 A set with more songs than the cue list has song cues gets, for each song after the last that has one, a copy of that song's cue, made with Copy To before anything else is written, numbered after that cue and every cue of its chain, and before the next cue: the next whole number when it is free, otherwise a decimal between the two. A follow or a hang Eos copies with the cue is taken off the copy, so the copy runs on into nothing, and the summary says so in a line after the line of the copy: `the follow`, `the hang`, or `the follow and the hang` with `took them off`. The copy then takes its own song's title and colour like any song cue, and the summary names each copy and the cue it is a copy of. A set with fewer songs leaves the other song cues as they are, `Song n` label included. A second run on the same weekly show file copies nothing and leaves the show as the first did.
 
-Song `n`'s colour comes from the one ProPresenter playlist whose name holds the date of the set, written as `November 15, 2026`, or with `--playlist <name>` from the one playlist of that whole name, by the same rule: from the picture of the first cue of the first presentation it links whose name is the song's title, by the same rule. With no playlist for the date or more than one, or with `--playlist` and no playlist of that name or more than one, nothing is written to Eos, the playlists it could mean are printed, one a line, each as `--playlist "<name>"`, and one line on stderr says why, exit 1. The colour is the hue of the most saturated of the picture's large areas that are not near black, never its mean, at the lights config's `saturation` and full brightness, and each song's line shows it as hue and as red, green and blue percentages, with the background file it came from, the label of the presentation's first slide.
+Song `n`'s colour comes from the one ProPresenter playlist whose name holds the date of the set, written as `November 15, 2026`, or with `--playlist <name>` from the one playlist of that whole name, by the same rule: from the picture of the first cue of the first presentation it links whose name is the song's title, by the same rule. With no playlist for the date or more than one, or with `--playlist` and no playlist of that name or more than one, nothing is written to Eos, the playlists it could mean are printed, one a line, each as `--playlist "<name>"`, and one line on stderr says why, exit 1. The colour is the hue of the most saturated of the picture's large areas, never its mean, at the lights config's `saturation` and full brightness, and each song's line shows it as hue and as red, green and blue percentages, with the background file it came from, the label of the presentation's first slide.
 
 There is no picture when it has no opaque pixel, when it has no large area that is not near black, when the most saturated of those areas is under 5% saturation, as ProPresenter's grey placeholder and a slide with no background are, when ProPresenter refuses it, or when it cannot be read. ProPresenter gives the placeholder for a picture it has not drawn yet, so the mode asks for a picture it did not get again, once a second, up to 5 times, and takes the first it gets. A song that still has no picture, and a song with no presentation in the playlist, keeps the template's colour: on each colour channel the colour its song cue had, recorded into the cue so the colour of the song before it does not track into it. Its line shows `template colour` and why: `no picture, <background file>`, `ProPresenter refused the picture (<status>), <background file>`, `the picture cannot be read, <background file>`, or `no presentation in the playlist "<playlist>"`, which also names each presentation of the playlist that ProPresenter did not give. Such a song takes about 5 seconds longer. A colour channel at intensity 0 in a song cue shows no colour there, so the summary warns of each one. A warning never stops the run and never sets exit 1.
 
