@@ -397,7 +397,7 @@ A song's colour comes from ProPresenter on the playback Mac, at the address in t
 
 The lights take the picture's hue and not its saturation. They take the hue at the `saturation` of `config/lights.json`, a number from 0 to 100, and at full brightness, because the backgrounds are pale and their own saturation reads as white light. A higher number gives a stronger colour and a lower one a paler colour. It is 80 to start: change it in the file and run the lights step again.
 
-No picture means the lights step found no colour to take: the picture has no opaque pixel, it has no large area that is not near black, or the most saturated of those areas is under 5% saturation. That is what ProPresenter's grey placeholder gives when the song's background file is not on the playback Mac, and what a first slide with no background gives. The song's line in the summary then reads `template colour  no picture, <background file>`, and the song cue keeps the template's colour, so the lights never show a guessed colour. To fix it, copy the background file the line names to the playback Mac, check that ProPresenter shows the background on the first slide of the song's presentation, and run the lights step again. A line that reads `template colour  no presentation in the playlist "<playlist>"` means the playlist does not link the song: link it (section 11) and run the lights step again.
+No picture means the lights step found no colour to take: the picture has no opaque pixel, or its most saturated large area is under 5% saturation. That is what ProPresenter's grey placeholder gives when the song's background file is not on the playback Mac, and what a first slide with no background gives. The song's line in the summary then reads `template colour  no picture, <background file>`, and the song cue keeps the template's colour, so the lights never show a guessed colour. To fix it, copy the background file the line names to the playback Mac, check that ProPresenter shows the background on the first slide of the song's presentation, and run the lights step again. A line that reads `template colour  no presentation in the playlist "<playlist>"` means the playlist does not link the song: link it (section 11) and run the lights step again.
 
